and preferred citing his own earlier papers \[**47**, p. 310\]. He had even less luck with the choice of assistant to write up results on contact transformations and partial differential equations. Felix Hausdorff's interests led him elsewhere, and Lie's thoughts on these subjects were never completely spelled out \[**16**, p. 324\]. Thus we may never discover the "true Lie".
